[38;2;124;124;124mTheorem (Takesaki / standard): Let T: A → B be a bounded linear map. Then T is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpositive iff T** is positive (where T**: A** → B** is the bitranspose, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124midentifying the double duals with enveloping von Neumann algebras).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mProof sketch: [0m
