[38;2;124;124;124mweak*. Then T**(a_α) = T(a_α) → T**(x) weak*. T(a_α) ∈ B+, and B+ is weak*-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mclosed in B** (since B**+ is the positive cone of the von Neumann algebra B**, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mwhich is weak*-closed, and B+ ⊆ B**+, but we need B**+ weak*-closed). Actually [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mB**+ is weak*-closed. So T**(x) = weak*-lim T(a_α) ∈ B**+.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe key step is: A+ is weak*-dense in A**+.[0m

